#X obj 667 11 hw.display;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 295 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Reads and sets the properties of the hardware display
(currently brightness only). The current value can be queried with
a bang or the @brightness? message \, and changed with the @brightness
message or by setting the @brightness property.;
#X text 240 168 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 193 • Automatic brightness control — adjusting the display
brightness from a patch \, for example fading it down in the evening
and up in the morning \, or linking it to an ambient light sensor.;
#X text 250 263 • Performance and installation scenarios — dimming
the display during a concert or an art installation \, so that the
screen does not distract the audience \, and restoring brightness when
the piece ends.;
#X text 240 333 Note: currently supported on macOS only.;
